# Local configuration and anything that could carry a credential.
# The pattern is deliberately wide: a file this repository does not name is not tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local.yml
*.local.yaml
*.local.properties
application-local.yml
application-local.yaml
application-secret*.yml
secrets/
*.pem
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
*-service-account*.json
credentials*.json

# Generated seed data -- see docs/decisions/publication-readiness.md PUB-7.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY TRACKS NO DATA FILE. The seed is produced by the generator in seed/,
# from a fixed seed value, so anyone can reproduce it. A committed dataset would be a
# dataset nobody could prove the provenance of, and the CI guard enforces the same rule
# from the other side so that a rename does not defeat it.
seed-out/
*.csv
*.tsv
*.jsonl
*.parquet
*.dump
*.bak
*.sql.gz

# Measurement output. Regenerated by the run that produced it; the NUMBERS live in
# docs/reports/, which is where a reader looks for them.
load/out/
*.gc.log
*.hprof
*.jfr

# Scratch
*.log
coverage/
.jacoco/
scratch/
tmp/

# `.study/` WAS IGNORED HERE AND IS NOT ANY MORE — removed 2026-08-14 on the PO's instruction.
#
#   It had two reasons. The first, that AGENTS.md requires repository documents to be in
#   English and those notes are Korean, is the PO's call and has been made.
#
#   THE SECOND HAS NOT GONE AWAY, and it was the load-bearing one: this repository is public,
#   and `git add -A` is used routinely in sessions here. A directory that is untracked but not
#   ignored is one careless stage away from being published, and `.study/` currently shows up
#   as `?? .study/` in every `git status`.
#
#   So the habit changes with the rule: while anything under `.study/` is meant to stay out of
#   a commit, staging is by explicit path. Publishing those notes is a separate decision from
#   un-ignoring them, and this line is not that decision.
